infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Internal module boundary vs network boundary
  desc The same seam costs almost nothing inside one deployable — and a fortune once it crosses the network
  compares
    - label Internal module boundary
      children
        - label Zero runtime cost
          desc A compile-time or test-time constraint, not a network hop
        - label Reshaped cheaply
          desc Experiment with the seam before any caller depends on it
        - label Extraction is mechanical
          desc Boundary already defined and tested — a split, not a redesign
    - label Network (service) boundary
      children
        - label Latency and failure modes
          desc Serialization overhead on every cross-module call
        - label Locked into contracts
          desc Encoded in API versions, pipelines, and team ownership
        - label Reshaped expensively
          desc A wrong seam needs API versioning, data migration, cross-team coordination
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f43f5e
